summary:
PASS. F-DG2-350 and F-DG2-351 are CLOSED_VERIFIED.
- F-DG2-350: my round-9 S10 repro now gives 404 for every media type. A new probe gives 404 + Connection: close for every Content-Type spelling and framing on unmatched routes, including a 10 GB Content-Length, Expect: 100-continue, never-ending chunked bodies and keep-alive smuggling. The body is never read and the hidden request never runs.
- F-DG2-351: the HTAB spelling is now accepted and stored byte-exact; the round-9 S11 assertion fails by design. Every refusal names the route's declared set, including the FST_ERR_CTP_INVALID_MEDIA_TYPE backstop. A 20,000-string fuzz found 0 mismatches between the decision and Fastify 5.6.1's parser lookup.
BE15 does not weaken bodyLimit, the strict UTF-8 parser, prototype-poisoning protection, CSRF, authorization, rate limiting, the 25 MiB streaming limit or the raw sha256. The D-070 tightenings do not affect the web client, which sends only bare media types.
All required checks ran and passed:
- build, typecheck, lint, openapi-lint (161), no-cdn, format;
- unit 765/765 on Node 22 and 24, and again under load;
- integration 570/570 in both locales, with 19 migrations applied;
- the AUD-403 sweep;
- historical validation of DG0 and DG1.
No new findings. Two observations are not raised, because neither is a BE15 regression: unmatched-route 404s are not rate-limited (pre-existing plugin behaviour, outside ADR-0007's 'every operation'), and light-my-request gives an AbortError for chunked over-limit inject (identical at 041478cb). No Critical, High or mandatory issue is unresolved.
